-- title:
--   Kernel of a scalar-compatible origin-chart map
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, viewed through its projective model: the graded ring $\mathrm{ProjModelRingCR}$ is the quotient of $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $W$, graded by `projModelGradingCR W`, whose degree-$n$ piece is the image of the homogeneous polynomials of degree $n$; `coord W i` denotes the class of $X_i$. The origin chart ring `OriginChartRing W` is the degree-zero homogeneous localisation `Away` of this graded ring at the degree-one element `coord W 1`, and `xOverY W`, `zOverY W` are the elements $X_0/X_1$ and $X_2/X_1$ of it, i.e. the classes of `coord W 0` and `coord W 2` over `coord W 1`. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from `OriginChartRing W` to $T$, and assume $\chi$ is scalar-compatible: for every $t \in T$, applying $\chi$ to the image of $t$ under the composite $T \to (\text{projModelGradingCR } W)\,0 \to$ `OriginChartRing W` (structure map into the degree-zero part, then `fromZeroRingHom`) returns $t$. The conclusion is that the kernel of $\chi$ is the ideal generated by the two elements $xOverY\,W - \iota(\chi(xOverY\,W))$ and $zOverY\,W - \iota(\chi(zOverY\,W))$, where $\iota$ denotes that same composite $T \to$ `OriginChartRing W`.
--
--   This identifies the kernel of a $T$-point of the origin chart of a Weierstrass model as the ideal of the point, generated by the two affine coordinates $X/Y$ and $Z/Y$ minus their values; it is the algebraic form of the statement that the chart is an affine plane curve through the given section. It is used in the analysis of the section at the origin and of the formal neighbourhood there, notably by the results computing the pushforward of this ideal and identifying the chart ring modulo it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_ker_eq_span_of_originChartRing.lean

